window.docContents[200].resolve({"/MoreStlc/#Type-Systems--MoreStlc___-More-on-the-Simply-Typed-Lambda-Calculus--Simple-Extensions-to-STLC--Numbers":{"contents":"\n\nAdding types, constants, and primitive operations for\nnatural numbers is easy (as we saw in the StlcExtended exercises).\n\n\n\nA more interesting extension... let-bindings.When writing a complex expression, it is often useful to give\nnames to some of its subexpressions: this avoids repetition and\noften increases readability.\n\nSyntax:\n\nt ::= \"...\"\n    | \"let\" x \"=\" t \"in\" t  (\"let-binding\") ;\n\n\nReduction:\n\n              t₁ ⟶ t₁'\n------------------------------------  (let₁)\nlet x = t₁ in t₂ ⟶ let x = t₁' in t₂\n\n-------------------------------       (letValue)\nlet x = v₁ in t₂ ⟶ [x := v₁] t₂\n\n\nTyping:\n\n       Γ ⊢ t₁ ⦂ τ₁\n  x ↦ τ₁ ; Γ ⊢ t₂ ⦂ τ₂\n-------------------------  (let)\nΓ ⊢ let x = t₁ in t₂ ⦂ τ₂\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009MoreStlc: More on the Simply Typed Lambda-Calculus\u0009Simple Extensions to STLC","header":"7.1.1. Numbers","id":"/MoreStlc/#Type-Systems--MoreStlc___-More-on-the-Simply-Typed-Lambda-Calculus--Simple-Extensions-to-STLC--Numbers"}});